# React Native (Expo) Coding Rules

## General
- Correctness and clarity over speed. Accessibility is required (`accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityRole`, touch target >= 44x44).
- Comments only explain *why*, never *what*.
- Add to existing files before creating new ones. Reuse before creating.
- No abbreviated variable names (`error` not `err`, `button` not `btn`).
- No generic `index.tsx` at a feature root; use explicit names. `index.ts` is allowed only as the barrel of a named component subfolder.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` for architecture, commands and workflow. Check Expo docs for the installed SDK before using any Expo/RN API.

## File Naming
| Type | Convention |
|------|-----------|
| Route (in `src/app`) | `kebab-case.tsx` / `[param].tsx` / `_layout.tsx` (Expo Router) |
| Component | `kebab-case.tsx`, exports `PascalCase` component |
| Hook | `use-kebab-case.ts` |
| API wrapper | `<feature>.api.ts` |
| Store | `<feature>.store.ts` |
| Schema | `<feature>.schema.ts` |
| Types | `<feature>.types.ts` |

## Exports
- Route files: default export (required by Expo Router).
- Everything else: named exports.
- Component subfolders (`components/<screen-name>/`) have an `index.ts` barrel re-exporting all named exports. Screens import from the barrel; files inside the same folder import each other relatively.

## Structure
- Feature code in `src/features/<feature>/`. Shared primitives in `src/components/ui/`. Infra in `src/lib/`.
- Route files in `src/app/` are thin shells: compose hooks + components, no business logic, no component definitions beyond the screen itself.
- No god screens: extract dialogs, sheets, list items and sections into their own files.

## Data Flow
- Screen owns API hooks (`useQuery` / `useMutation`) and passes data + callbacks via props.
- Presentational components do not call React Query hooks or the API directly.
- Never fetch inside list item components.

## API & Services
- Use only `api` from `@/lib/api` and `unwrap` for `ApiResponse<T>`. No other axios instances, no raw `fetch` to the backend.
- API wrappers are plain objects (not classes), return unwrapped data, and do not catch errors — let React Query surface them.
- Before writing any form/api/schema, read the BE Command, Validator and `*Response.cs`. Field names match the BE DTO exactly (camelCase, no aliases). Every `NotEmpty`/`MaximumLength`/`MinimumLength`/`GreaterThan`/`EmailAddress` rule has a zod equivalent. Send only the fields the Command declares; never omit required ones. Response types include every field the BE returns.
- Update order when BE changes: schema -> types -> api -> hook -> component.
- Never hard-code hosts; use `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL`. Never put secrets in `EXPO_PUBLIC_*`.

## Auth & Security
- Tokens only in `expo-secure-store` via `token-storage`. Never log tokens, passwords or personal data.
- Permission codes are centralised in one config file; components never compare raw permission strings. Backend remains the source of truth.

## State Management
- Server state -> TanStack Query. Query keys are arrays: `['resource', params]`. Handle `onError` in mutations.
- Client/UI state -> zustand (`*.store.ts`), select with selectors (`useAuth((s) => s.signedIn)`), never subscribe to the whole store needlessly.
- Never mutate state directly. Minimise `useEffect`; derive during render. Effects with subscriptions/timers/listeners (SignalR, camera, keyboard) must clean up.

## Forms
- react-hook-form + zod. Define the zod schema first and infer the TS type (`z.infer`).
- Schemas live in `<feature>.schema.ts` and export the zod schema plus its inferred type. The screen calls `useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) })`; components receive `form` as a prop and never call `useForm` themselves.
- Separate Create vs Update schemas when BE commands differ. Field errors from `formState.errors`. No manual validation when zod can express it.
- Set proper `keyboardType`, `autoCapitalize`, `returnKeyType`, `secureTextEntry`; wrap forms with keyboard avoidance.

## Error Handling
- Never swallow errors silently. Log via a central logger (no stray `console.log` in committed code) and show user feedback (inline message/toast/alert).
- Every async screen handles loading, error and success (empty state too). Use early returns for loading/error.
- Network failure and 401/403 are normal cases on mobile — handle them explicitly.

## Styling
- Use `StyleSheet.create`; no inline style objects in hot paths. Use theme tokens from `@/constants/theme` / `useTheme`, not hard-coded colours (support light and dark).
- Respect safe areas (`react-native-safe-area-context`). Test small and large screens, and font scaling.
- Platform-specific code via `*.ios.tsx` / `*.android.tsx` / `Platform.select`, kept minimal.

## Performance
- Long lists: `FlatList`/`FlashList` with `keyExtractor`; stable `renderItem` (`useCallback`) and memoised rows (`React.memo`) when rows are non-trivial.
- Avoid anonymous heavy work in render; memoise only when profiling or list rows justify it.
- Images via `expo-image`, sized explicitly.
- Do not block the JS thread with large synchronous work.

## TypeScript
- No `any`; use `unknown` and narrow. No `as Type` unless unavoidable (comment why).
- `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases. Use `import type` for type-only imports.
- Derive types from the source of truth (`z.infer`, `ReturnType`, `Awaited`). Avoid enums — use `as const` objects or `z.enum()`.
- Props typed with explicit interfaces, destructured in the signature. Optional props use `?`, not manual `| undefined`; use `readonly` for props/state that must not be mutated.

## Dependencies & Native
- Package manager is pnpm. Add packages with `pnpm exec expo install <pkg>`, never `pnpm add`. Prefer Expo modules.
- Never edit `ios/` or `android/`; use `app.json` + config plugins. Native-module libs need a development build (not Expo Go).

## Definition of Done
- `pnpm exec expo lint` and `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` pass for the files you touched.
- Behaviour verified (on emulator/device when it involves native features) — say so explicitly if it could not be run.
